  "id": "COMPOUND:4112 - PROTEIN:1503",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which S-sulphocysteine may influence G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, through a series of target interactions. The drug is implicated in targeting Cytochrome c4, which is then a target of two different compounds—6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin and 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin—both of which ultimately act on G1/S-specific cyclin-D1. This indicates a possible pathway where S-sulphocysteine may serve as a modulator or inhibitor of the downstream targets, potentially affecting cyclin-D1 expression or activity. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same downstream target suggests that S-sulphocysteine may exert its effects through a mechanism that is not directly linked to cyclin-D1, but rather through a broader network of interactions that ultimately influence its expression. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between S-sulphocysteine and G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
